From 21fa1a6cc944c06120b14ab788907e528f0ff561 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chai <tsaitomd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:08:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: the fused prompt-chunk kernel

When a sparse call's partials would not fit the pool (cuda_latent.fuses), one
block handles a (row, HB heads) and loops the row's chunks, merging in the
kernel, so the prompt chunk costs one launch and no partial buffer. The fused
form is sparse only: a dense block has no counts to walk, so it traps.

fetch8 and store8 move out of chunks_wide into namespace-scope templates in
common/mla.cuh, so both read the E4M3 cache through one implementation. A
prefill now funds one dense pass's partials instead of every sparse call's,
which is what makes fuses() reachable.

Measured on one GB10 pair: base and patched images started alternately, three
cold prefill runs per start; the PR body carries the table. glm-ref, the greedy
token hashes and the 35,941-token token_sha are unchanged.
